projects.description:
The Forest Avenue project was originally developed from the 2021 Facility Condition Assessment, which estimated approximately $6.24 million in improvements.  Since that time, the project team has completed schematic design, further evaluated the existing building, developed the project scope in greater detail, and reconciled construction pricing using current subcontractor and market information.
Based on that work, the project team has developed an updated Forest Avenue project budget of $7,469,000.  This is the first time this updated budget is being formally presented to the Town Council.
The $7,469,000 project includes substantial renovations necessary to address the condition, accessibility, life-safety requirements and long-term use of the Forest Avenue facility, including:
•	renovation of six existing multi-user restrooms;
•	replacement of exterior windows in the original 1957 building and 1994 addition;
•	replacement of classroom unit ventilators and associated HVAC improvements;
•	installation of a complete fire sprinkler system and new fire service;
•	replacement of approximately 8,000 square feet of lower-level flooring, including moisture mitigation;
•	replacement of the existing non-compliant LULA elevator with a new code-compliant elevator;
•	ADA accessibility improvements throughout the facility;
•	playground improvements; and
•	installation of a new monument sign.
The reconciled construction estimate supporting this scope was approximately $5.8 million, with the balance of the project budget consisting of professional services, project expenses and contingencies.
